nt state updates form execution trace.", "N7_Validator": "WEAK_EVIDENCE: Latent execution as approximate validation.", "N8_ComposerRouter": "WEAK_EVIDENCE: Sequential statement composition.", "N9_VersionedRegistry": "NO_EVIDENCE"}, "claim_support_status": "PARTIAL", "source_specific_reasoning": "S120-017 provides novel evidence for N6 (ExecutionTrace) and N5 (Interpreter): the latent execution module approximates program execution in a differentiable latent space, enabling partial program synthesis. The latent state updates form a primitive execution trace. This is a unique contribution \u2014 most other papers do not model execution at all. However, the latent execution is approximate, not formal, and no exact equivalence or verification is provided.", "comparison_to_provisional": "NARROWS", "comparison_reason": "High review reveals latent execution contribution not likely captured in provisional card.", "reviewer_model": "qclaw/pool-glm-5.2-night", "reviewer_reasoning_level": "high", "reviewed_at": "2026-07-13T19:40:00Z", "supersedes_provisional_card_id": "S120-017-provisional-121"}
