    "classification_statistics": "The supervised code evaluates NUM_TEST_POINTS=600, fixes NumPy and Python random seeds to 1 and computes 95-percent intervals as 1.96*sample-standard-deviation/sqrt(600). The paper labels the table intervals as 95-percent confidence intervals over tasks but does not state 600 in the paper text.",
    "reinforcement_learning": "Evaluate 2D navigation plus cheetah/ant velocity and direction tasks with two-layer 100-unit ReLU policies. Inner updates use vanilla policy gradient; the meta-optimizer uses TRPO. Two-dimensional navigation trains with one inner update and 20 trajectories; locomotion uses horizon 200 and generally 20 rollouts per step, with 40 for ant direction. Main evidence is learning curves rather than numerical tables.",
    "reinforcement_learning_selection": "The supplement says evaluation uses alpha=0.1 for the first step and 0.05 later because it performed better, comparator step sizes are manually tuned per domain, and the best average return during up to 500 meta-iterations is selected for evaluation. No separate model-selection validation protocol is defined.",
    "negative_or_omitted_results": "Random-initialization goal-velocity curves are omitted because returns are below -200 for cheetah and below -25 for ant. Omitting them from plots is disclosed but reduces direct visual comparison. The main plots do not provide numerical tables, seeds, run counts or clearly defined uncertainty bands.",
    "context_vector_supplement": "A learned context-vector alternative scores Omniglot 94.9+-0.9/97.7+-0.3 versus MAML 98.7+-0.4/99.9+-0.1; on cheetah direction it remains around -40 to -42 while MAML reaches 293.19, 313.48 and 315.65 after later steps. This is a distinct baseline, not an adapter implementation of MAML.",
    "released_supervised_artifact": "The current repository includes source code and a later 2018 MiniImageNet checkpoint. It has no requirements lock, paper-run raw results, complete paper checkpoints, test suite, CI, seed ledger or immutable release tying reported tables to code. Syntax compilation succeeded but the TensorFlow 1.x experiments were not executed.",
    "released_rl_artifact": "The RL repository retains paper-deadline history, experiment code, plots and 39 data-like files under icml, including small aggregate result pickles and some roughly 0.8-1.1 MB path pickles. Its environment pins several old packages/SHAs but leaves other dependencies and the external MuJoCo runtime incompletely pinned. These artifacts improve provenance but do not form a complete reproducible experiment receipt.",
    "reproducibility": "Public code is valuable and a paper-deadline RL commit exists, but exact present-day reproduction is blocked by old frameworks, incomplete environment pinning, missing complete original checkpoints/raw trials/seeds and ambiguous paper-to-repository state."
  },
  "uncertainty_model": "Tasks, examples, trajectories, transition dynamics and stochastic policies are probabilistic objects, and the reported classification intervals quantify task-sampling variation under the evaluation code. MAML itself emits point parameters and predictions/policies; it does not define calibrated epistemic uncertainty, predictive posterior semantics or uncertainty-aware admission. Sine and RL plots lack sufficient run-level uncertainty metadata, while selected best-training iterates and tuned evaluation step sizes add selection uncertainty not propagated into reported curves.",
  "lifecycle_and_provenance": "The conceptual lifecycle is meta-initialization, meta-training over tasks, checkpoint theta, support-set adaptation to ephemeral theta'_i and query evaluation/deployment. The paper and repositories do not define immutable identities for the task distribution, dataset snapshot, environment, initialization, adapted artifact or evaluation receipt. The supervised code saves TensorFlow checkpoints and CSV/pickle test outputs, but its public history began after arXiv [AXIS_CODE] and later changed. The October 2017 commit 617ba8a explicitly fixed swapped Omniglot validation/test selection; evidence does not establish which code state or flag generated the published table, so this is a provenance risk rather than proof of an affected result. No registry records lineage, compatibility, approvals, monitoring, deprecation, migration, rollback or tombstones for adapted functions.",
  "function_os_node_impacts": {
    "N1_FunctionSpec": {
